A||||3||Digisys||Temperature Gauge Not working correctly !||||9||
Z||000000||Digisys||10-03-2001||06:55 AM||||For those who helped me resolve my valve lash problem thanks, especially to 87GTZ34<BR>for the suggestions. The car is back together and running great except for one problem. Since I got it back running the Temperature Gauge is not working correctly. When you start the car the gauge jumps to the 100 deg mark and thats where it stays, it does not move again till you shut the car off.<BR> Any ideas ?||||reg||9
Z||000001||fiero_nightmare||10-03-2001||07:07 AM||||to me it either sounds like a short in the wires or a bad gauge. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||10-03-2001||06:34 PM||||You may want to try replacing the sending unit.  It is usually a brass thingy, trunk-left side, right underneath the ignition coil, with a couple of wires sticking out of it (on the V6, anyway).  They're not that expensive - I've had a cracked one and usually gave me a false temp.<P>If that doesn't work, it's probably the gauge or a bad wire (unlikely).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||10-03-2001||07:20 PM||||My 87 GT had the same problem and it was the sending unit.  I forget where it is located exactly but it is on the top of the engine.  Pull off the connector, then take a paper clip and ground both terminals to the block.  If the idiot light comes on and the gauge shoots up then it is most likely the sending unit.  Simple enough.||||reg||1
